# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL connection string. Required only if using custom backend features.
# Currently not needed for v1 launch (auth + contact deferred to future).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname

# ── Admin (deferred) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated emails allowed into the internal /api/admin/* routes
# (server/admin.ts). Only consulted once AUTH_ENABLED and ADMIN_ENABLED
# are flipped on in server/routes.ts; unset means nobody is an admin.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=founder@example.com

# ── Email (Resend) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get your API key at https://resend.com
# Without this key, emails are logged to console in development mode.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Shopify Headless ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED for production. See SHOPIFY_SETUP.md for full setup instructions.
# Both variables must be set together for Shopify integration to activate.
# Without them, the site uses local mock product data (in "mock" mode only).
#
# Your .myshopify.com domain (no https://)
# SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=turath-collective.myshopify.com
#
# Storefront API access token (from your Shopify app settings)
# SHOPIFY_STOREFRONT_TOKEN=shpat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Shopify mode controls fallback behavior when API is unavailable:
#   "live"  - Production mode: Fail if Shopify unavailable, no fallback to mock data
#   "mock"  - Development mode: Fallback to mock data silently when API unavailable
# Default: "mock" (safe for development)
# VITE_SHOPIFY_MODE=mock

# ── Analytics (Google Analytics 4) ───────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Get your Measurement ID from your GA4 property settings.
# When not set, analytics are silently disabled (no console errors).
# Format: G-XXXXXXXXXX
# VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# ── Error monitoring (Sentry) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Public DSN from the Sentry project's client-keys settings — it is
# baked into the client bundle by design and is not a secret. Unset means
# monitoring is off, which is the normal local state.
# Sentry is inside the consent scope: it starts only after the visitor accepts
# the banner, never before (client/src/lib/monitoring.ts).
# The DSN's region host must already be allowed by connect-src in
# worker/security-headers.ts (us / de / plain ingest.sentry.io are).
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://xxxxxxxx@oNNNNNN.ingest.us.sentry.io/NNNNNN
#
# Worker-side errors go to a SEPARATE Sentry project via SENTRY_DSN (no VITE_
# prefix — it is runtime config read from the Cloudflare env, not baked into
# the bundle). Set it in wrangler.toml [vars] for production and .dev.vars
# locally. Unlike the browser SDK this one is NOT consent-gated: it records our
# own infrastructure failing, not visitor behaviour. See worker/index.ts.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://xxxxxxxx@oNNNNNN.ingest.us.sentry.io/NNNNNN

# ── Demo mode (LOCAL DEV ONLY — NEVER SET IN VERCEL) ─────────────────────────
# Master switch for the founder's own .env.local: forces mock products,
# placeholder reviews/social proof, the shipping promo (placeholder $75
# threshold if none set), and the full site instead of the coming-soon page,
# so the complete intended experience is previewable in one local run.
# NEVER set this in any Vercel environment (dev, test, or main) — a deployed
# build would show fake reviews, fake social posts, and a fake shipping offer
# to real visitors. See client/src/lib/flags.ts.
# VITE_DEMO_MODE=true

# ── UI feature flags (build-time, baked by Vite) ─────────────────────────────
# Shipping promo: ONE gate for both the announcement bar above the navbar and
# the free-shipping progress bar in the cart drawer. OFF by default — the copy
# claims a free-shipping offer that has no finalized pricing/shipping policy
# behind it yet. Only set to "true" once pricing is decided AND the
# announcement copy (locales */common.json → "announcement") and the shipping
# policy page state the same, true threshold. Both surfaces also need
# VITE_FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD (the real CAD amount) — neither renders while
# either variable is missing.
# VITE_SHOW_SHIPPING_PROMO=true
# VITE_FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD=100
